WEBVTT

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.670
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:32.400
...the instant I look away.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.540
I just kept counting...

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.980
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:50.350
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:56.290
In this time that seems so dry,

00:01:56.230 --> 00:02:01.400
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:07.260
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.310
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:19.980
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:27.810
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.350
Dojima, you must be tired from working so late again last night.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.700
I'm fine.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.860
Yurika.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.830
Can you head out right away?

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.300
I have to get to work on that violent death from last night.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.570
Huh? But...

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.470
You'll be fine. I'll leave you to continue the investigation.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.540
Are you sure that's such a good idea...?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.610
I've kept the Administrator informed as to our situation here,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.120
...but all he ever says is that he'll let us look after things here,

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.950
...and he never even shows his face around here.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.720
I wonder if he's gone to the Factory again?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.380
Well, that's what he said...

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.520
But what the hell is really going on?

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.070
I don't know.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.900
You're talking about news from the Boss, right?

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.000
I've heard the same.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:07.170
I don't know any more than what you've heard, Chief.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.770
I should get going.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.110
Miss Karasuma, I'll go with you.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.050
You should...

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.040
Sakaki, we need you to stay here.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.880
If anything happened here, we'd be in a real jam.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.350
Just looking out for your own necks, huh?

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.820
Nobody's said it even once this past month.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.800
"If only Amon were here..."

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.720
Right.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.520
I've been keeping an eye on things for a while, but I want you to resume Orbo production.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.730
As for Amon, headquarters only gives me their usual answer.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.640
That's right.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.570
It looks like headquarters still doesn't know where Robin is.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.910
They haven't issued a search order for her.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.900
Well, as to that...

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.440
Yes, they could locate her at any time if they wanted to.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:26.180
But it's obvious that their objective was the Orbo.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.490
She was just an excuse for them.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.050
In any case, I want you to check up on headquarters' activities.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.590
Right. I'll leave you to it.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:08.000
Yeah, don't you think so, too?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.330
I knew it all along!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.160
Yes, that's right.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.000
And yesterday, Mrs. Kato's husband also...

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.440
Excuse me.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.370
I have a delivery.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:23.840
From the Nagira Law Office.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.410
Just a moment, please.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.680
Wait over there.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.420
Your regular delivery from Mr. Nagira has arrived, sir.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:40.590
Yes, sir.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.990
Yes, sir. It seems that way.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.770
Now, now, don't do that.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.580
Yes, sir. I understand.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.920
I'll see to it.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.990
Yes, sir. Sorry to bother you.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.380
I'm sorry that took so long.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.430
I've been told to sign for it here.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.540
Thank you.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.870
Um... Nice bike.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.920
Nagira Law Offices

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.130
She's taking longer than usual to get back today, don't you think?

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.620
You think so?

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:03.930
You don't suppose that young girlfriend of yours has run off, do you?

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.130
Girlfriend?

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.540
Hana, if anything happens, give me a call.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.520
I'm gonna go buy some cigarettes.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.120
You should at least try to get some work done.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.590
All you've been doing lately is chasing after girls.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.530
I don't chase after them. They're the ones who come after me.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:28.990
Right?

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.430
Whatever.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.470
Geez...

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.730
See you later!

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.450
You've been sneaking around, spying on us...

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.060
Let her go.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:10:59.540
Somebody...

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:30.540
Dojima! Hurry up and call in!

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.020
Robin...?

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:38.460
Wait! Wait, Robin!

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.420
Pretty pathetic, huh?

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.380
A Witch hunter getting hunted by a Witch...

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.820
I was chasing after some missing Seeds.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:15.360
At some point, they started tailing me instead.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.830
They weren't the ones I was after.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.630
But there's probably a connection somewhere.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.640
Hey, Dojima, how is everyone?

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.270
We're fine.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:31.310
The people who attacked us used plastic bullets.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.540
So aside from Sakaki, who broke his leg, we're all back up and running.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:39.510
Still, it's crazy to expect us to hunt like we did before without you or Amon.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.220
What about Amon? Where is he?

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.290
We haven't been told anything.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.780
We figured that he might be with you, Robin.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.450
But I guess not.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.360
Then Amon isn't...

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:54.100
Zaizen hasn't shown up at the office since the attack, either.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.030
What the heck is going on?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.440
I've been trying to figure that out this whole time.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.510
Why me...?

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.790
Why do I have to be chased down by my own organization?

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:16.820
You can relax, though.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.280
The STN-J hasn't gotten any orders to hunt you, Robin.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.660
I'm not sure how long that'll be the case, though.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.260
But I'm really glad you made it out okay. Honestly.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.130
About Amon...

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.160
Amon saved me.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:37.040
Oh, he did? Everyone will be happy to hear that!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:41.040
Don't. Don't tell them. Not about Amon, or about me.

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.850
All right, I promise.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.650
But... But do you think you can help me out?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:50.750
Help me out again like you did.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:55.630
Sakaki's been sidelined, and Miho is desperately trying to fill Amon's shoes.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.660
I might be sent out on a hunt by myself again.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:02.640
Robin... If that happens, will you come with me?

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:03.630
That's impossible.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.270
I can't tell you how to reach me.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:10.710
Besides, if you get mixed up with me, I know I'll cause you nothing but trouble.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:12.370
Robin...

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:27.160
Dojima, have you heard anything about that day? Anything at all?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.970
Now that you mention it, Michael...

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:31.800
What?

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.770
Apparently, an Orbo gun and some data were stolen that day.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:39.960
Michael says that at least the data is secure thanks to his security program.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:41.800
What does that mean?

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:46.880
Robin...

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.250
Thank you. I'm serious.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.140
Oh, welcome back.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.670
Mr. Nagira was worried about you.

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.750
I stopped for some coffee.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.080
If you're going to be late, you should call and tell us!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.710
I'm sorry.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.380
I delivered the package, though.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.160
If you had some coffee, you don't need any tea, then, right?

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.730
No, I'm fine.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.030
She could at least sit and chat for a while...

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:41.440
Geez, kids nowadays...

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.300
What does Mr. Nagira see in her, anyway?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.660
Oh, well, he'll get bored with her soon enough.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.080
Robin, the next time I see you...

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.560
I'll wait for you.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:50.100
But I don't want to just wait and do nothing.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.380
I've cornered him.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.380
The Factory is already on its way.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:05.480
Roger.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:08.820
Don't do anything reckless, Miss Karasuma!

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:15.030
Are you listening, Miss Karasuma?!

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:15.920
Mr. Nagira would like to see you.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.890
He wants to know if you'd like some dinner.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.560
So? Did something happen?

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.070
Not really.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:33.630
You know, I was the one that said it would be best for you to hide in the city.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.770
But you're asking for trouble if you forget what kind of situation you're in.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:38.980
As if I could ever forget.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.850
If you slip up, you'll put me in danger as well.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:45.150
I only took you in because Amon asked me to.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.950
I have no intention of risking my life to protect you, got it?

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:52.920
I bumped into someone from the STN-J.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.890
"Bumped into"? Did you talk?

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.270
I didn't tell her anything.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:02.460
But I thought I might be able to learn something about Amon.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.700
He'll contact you. Didn't I say that was the deal?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.200
Oh, well. There was something else I wanted to talk to you about.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:14.340
Take a look at this.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:25.790
Is this man Zaizen, the boss of the STN-J?

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.530
Touko...

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.170
You know her?

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.360
She was my roommate.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:39.070
She got involved in a shootout because of me.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.940
I see. She's in a sanatorium right now.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.780
Physically, she's made a full recovery,

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:46.910
...but the shock has apparently made her mentally unstable.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.280
I don't know for sure, but it's probably no big deal.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.710
They're just being extra careful because she's Zaizen's only daughter.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.090
Daughter?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.250
You didn't know?

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:59.720
She has a different last name because he and her mother divorced,

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.730
...but they're father and daughter, all right.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:04.890
I don't get it... Why didn't Touko say anything?

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:06.320
Beats me.

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:08.800
Nothing makes sense anymore...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.800
I can't... trust anyone.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.680
Other than Amon, you mean?

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:21.280
I don't know about it myself,

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.350
...but this Zaizen guy is a real piece of work.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:29.690
Nagira... Are you digging into the STN-J because you have some other objective?

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.820
Not just because of me and Amon?

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:34.490
Objective? It's nothing like that.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.500
I hate people who slap labels like "Witch" or "Seed" on folks...

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.800
...and then try to tie 'em to a stake.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.710
It seems different now.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:58.890
You think so?

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:00.790
Not just you, Miss Karasuma.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.680
It seems like everyone has changed.

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.160
Yes, I suppose we have...

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:11.530
Welcome.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:13.630
Good work.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:15.230
You, too.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:21.070
You look exhausted. Would you like something sweet?

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.440
You did really well today.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:26.340
I think I'll be able to head out with you tomorrow.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.780
Assuming that nothing happens before then.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.910
You're strong.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:33.220
I'm not strong at all. I'm scared, too.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:37.020
Out of all of us, I might be the one who's the most frightened and insecure.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:41.330
It feels like I'll go crazy if I think too much, so that's why I'm always on the move.

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:44.830
I knew it, I just can't hold it in! I have to tell you...

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:46.560
You should hear this, too, Master.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.640
What's the matter?

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:53.370
I was rescued today... By Robin.

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:57.070
Robin... She's okay.

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:03.440
Thank goodness... I'm so glad...

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:45.010
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:47.870
Tell me.

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:59.860
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:09.750
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:14.240
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:19.610
...all those promises...

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:26.010
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:31.810
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.590
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
